# Tests and snippet cases of `vkxp-binding` that cannot pass over Ruby 1.9.2 yet.
#
# An entry is a reason, written as comment lines, followed by one or more lines
# `test <binary> <name>` (the name of the test file, or `lib` for a unit test, and the name
# of the test as `vkxp-binding` prints it) or `case <name>` (a snippet case of `tests/cases`
# or `tests/scene_cases`). Entries are separated by blank lines. A listed test carries the
# marker `pending_over_ruby_1_9_2!()`, is run alone and counts as passed only while it fails;
# when it passes, the run fails until the entry and the marker are removed.
#
# A reason is one of three kinds and names its source: behaviour of RGSS1 or RGSS2 that a
# section of a measurement report says RGSS3 does differently ("V0 report" is
# `ace-v0-REPORT.md`, "API report" is `ace-v1-api-REPORT.md` of the measurements of the
# original runtime, which are kept outside the repository); a construct of Ruby 1.8 that
# Ruby 1.9 has differently; the symbol numbering of Ruby 1.8.1. A crash, a hang, a value
# lost under collector stress or a wrong pixel is a fault and is never listed.

# The message of Ruby itself for a wrong count of arguments of a method with a fixed arity:
# `wrong number of arguments (2 for 1)` in Ruby 1.8, without the space in Ruby 1.9.2
# (`wrong number of arguments(2 for 1)`). The messages the binding words itself do not
# differ.
test lib foundation_tests::a_wrong_count_raises_argument_error
test scene_rgss2 the_readers_return_the_object_given_and_other_objects_are_refused
case wrong number of arguments

# `Float#inspect` of Ruby 1.8 prints 15 significant digits (`1.18059162071741e+21`); Ruby
# 1.9 prints the shortest text that reads back as the same number
# (`1180591620717411300000.0`).
test lib foundation_tests::floats_convert_from_any_number

# Changing a frozen object raises `TypeError` in Ruby 1.8 and `RuntimeError` in Ruby 1.9.
test lib foundation_tests::a_failure_to_name_the_class_of_a_wrong_argument_is_raised_after_destructors_ran

# `String#==` of Ruby 1.9 is false for a UTF-8 literal and an ASCII-8BIT string that hold the
# same bytes outside ASCII; a string of Ruby 1.8 has no encoding. The probe of the test
# returns bytes.
test lib foundation_tests::strings_convert_and_invalid_utf8_is_replaced

# `String#+` of Ruby 1.9 refuses a UTF-8 literal with bytes outside ASCII and an ASCII-8BIT
# string (`Encoding::CompatibilityError`); the snippet builds a dump that way, which Ruby
# 1.8 joins as bytes.
case data written by the original runtime

# `Module#public_instance_methods` and `Module#constants` return Strings in Ruby 1.8 and
# Symbols in Ruby 1.9; the tests compare them with lists of Strings.
test arity_rgss2 no_class_has_a_method_the_list_lacks
test modules button_constants

# `Marshal.dump` of Ruby 1.9 writes the encoding of a string as an instance variable: the
# dump of a UTF-8 string that a `_dump` method returned is six bytes longer than in Ruby
# 1.8, and the test expects the size of Ruby 1.8.
test stress a_dumped_string_survives_a_collection_while_it_is_written

# `$!` after a `rescue` clause has ended: Ruby 1.8 puts back the error that was current
# before, Ruby 1.9 leaves `nil`. How RGSS3 starts over is another matter (API report 1.3).
test run_game a_rescue_in_the_run_after_a_reset_leaves_the_reset

# The tests expect the globals of RGSS1 and RGSS2, `$KCODE` of `"UTF8"` and an empty load
# path. On the original runtime of RGSS3 `$KCODE` is `nil` (API report 0, row "kernel"; V0
# report 8) and the load path is `["."]` (V0 report 2, API report 1.1).
test prelude globals_are_those_of_the_original_runtime
test run_game the_first_script_sees_the_prepared_globals

# The tests hold the symbol numbering of Ruby 1.8.1 and read it with `Symbol#to_i`, which
# Ruby 1.9 does not have. Ruby 1.9.2 numbers its symbols as the release does, and a dump
# does not depend on the numbers (API report 4.2).
test run_game_first_uses the_first_uses_move_the_sequence_as_on_the_original
test run_game_lazy_names a_new_name_has_the_measured_number_after_every_step_of_the_probe
test run_game_rgss2 the_first_script_of_a_game_of_vx_sees_the_measured_numbers_and_frame
test run_game_symbols the_first_local_variables_of_the_first_script_have_the_measured_numbers
